# Amaken Web Application - System Design

This document describes the high-level system design and architecture of the Amaken Web Application based on the current implementation.

## 1. High-Level Architecture
The application uses a modern decoupled architecture, with a **Next.js frontend** speaking to an **ERPNext/Frappe backend** via REST APIs.

```mermaid
graph TD
    Client[Web Browser / Client]
    
    subgraph Frontend [Next.js Application]
        UI[UI Components - Radix/Tailwind]
        State[Next.js App Router]
        DataFetch[API Route Handlers / Server Actions]
    end
    
    subgraph Backend [ERPNext / Frappe]
        API[Frappe REST APIs]
        DocTypes[Frappe DocTypes]
        DB[(MariaDB)]
    end
    
    Client -->|HTTP/HTTPS| State
    State -->|Page Renders| Client
    State --> UI
    UI -->|Trigger Actions| DataFetch
    DataFetch -->|Fetch / POST Data| API
    API -->|Read/Write| DocTypes
    DocTypes --> DB
```

## 2. Frontend Module Structure
The frontend application is structured around various core business domains, built with Next.js App Router for optimized routing and layout sharing.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    AppRouter((App Router))
    
    AppRouter --> Group[Group]
    AppRouter --> RealEstate[Real Estate]
    AppRouter --> Appraisal[Appraisal]
    AppRouter --> Consultation[Consultation]
    AppRouter --> Portal[Portal / Auth]
    
    subgraph Group [Group Module]
        G_Projects[Projects Directory]
        G_Auctions[Auctions Directory]
        G_Units[Units Directory]
    end
    
    subgraph RealEstate [Real Estate Module]
        RE_Listings[Property Listings]
    end
```

## 3. Data Flow (Lead Generation Example)
One of the core interactions is lead capture, like registering interest for a property. Here's how data flows across the system boundaries:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant FrontendUI as UnitInterestModal (Client)
    participant NextAPI as Next.js API (/api/lead)
    participant ERPNext as ERPNext API Backend
    
    User->>FrontendUI: Fills form & Submits
    FrontendUI->>FrontendUI: Zod Validation
    FrontendUI->>NextAPI: POST Application JSON
    NextAPI->>NextAPI: Secure/format payload
    NextAPI->>ERPNext: POST to custom Frappe endpoint (Lead)
    ERPNext->>ERPNext: Validate & Create Lead DocType
    ERPNext-->>NextAPI: 200 OK + Lead ID
    NextAPI-->>FrontendUI: 200 Success
    FrontendUI-->>User: Show Toast / Success Message
```

## 4. Key Technologies
* **Framework:** Next.js 15+ (App Router focused)
* **Language:** TypeScript
* **Styling:** Tailwind CSS + PostCSS
* **Component Library:** shadcn/ui (Radix UI + Lucide Icons)
* **State & Forms:** React Hook Form, Zod (Schema Validation)
* **Backend Interaction:** `frappe-react-sdk` and standard fetch/REST methods to ERPNext.

## 5. Domain Models (Backend Mapping)
The system represents physical and business concepts structurally linked together:

```mermaid
erDiagram
    PROJECT ||--o{ UNIT : contains
    PROJECT {
        string name
        string description
        string status
    }
    UNIT ||--o| AUCTION : "may partcipate in"
    UNIT {
        string unit_name
        float numeric_value
        string status
        string marketing_type
    }
    AUCTION {
        string auction_name
        datetime start_date
        datetime end_date
    }
    LEAD ||--o| UNIT : "interested in"
    LEAD {
        string contact_name
        string mobile_number
    }
```
